<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48594" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			(with and without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς</span>) <i>sacred
				ship, which carried the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωροί</span> to their destination, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.87
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				314
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστολος θ</span>., of
				<i>Charon's bark</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				858
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span>) <i>road by which the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωροί</span>
			<i>went</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> pl.,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάκχαι</span>, Id., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.25.12
			</span></i>; of attendants of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				9.261
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
